# Freeze 50 v1.1(c), FT-A24(v): the fusion-tax companion frontier table is a
# deterministic function of committed inputs, carries no row that carries a
# claim, and is regenerated by the probe. The committed results file carries
# its SHA-256 and accounts for every omitted row.
walt-factory/results/fusion_tax_frontier_*.txt
# SR-A22(iii)(d): the second-rung companion per-(I,b,J) table, on the same
# terms — regenerable, no row carrying a claim, and the committed results file
# carries its SHA-256, byte and line counts plus per-unit accounting integers.
walt-factory/results/second_rung_frontier_*.txt
# Freeze 54(d), SS-A4(e): the seed survey's fat artifacts — the companion
# frontier table and the checkpoint blocks — are gitignored BY LOCATION rather
# than by pattern. They are written OUT OF TREE under
# /Users/jason/data/texas-42/seed-survey (run-owner amendment, 2026-08-15) so a
# worktree can be deleted without losing run data. The committed summary
# walt-factory/results/seed_survey_*.txt carries their absolute paths, the
# companion's SHA-256, byte and line counts, and per-unit accounting integers,
# and those are the only link between the repository and that data. Nothing of
# the seed survey's fat side is ever written inside this tree, so there is no
# pattern to ignore here; this comment is the record of that decision.
